# `__PROJECT_NAME__`

A Maximus backend on Cloudflare Workers, with Vite+ as its default toolchain. `GET /` returns **Hello World**, `/health` reports liveness,
and `/api/openapi.json` describes the API. `GET /api/v1/greeting` is authenticated. The starter refuses
production tokens until an identity provider or verified resolver is configured in maximus.config.ts.

## Development

Install dependencies with `bun install`, then run `bun run dev`. The local development token is in
the ignored `.dev.vars` file. It is accepted only on localhost and is excluded from production builds.
`bun run verify` generates types, checks TypeScript, lint and formatting, and builds. It runs no tests.

## Structure

The [Maximus project layout](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus/blob/main/docs/guides/project-structure.md)
uses optional directories. Add only the modules the service needs:

| Directory        | Convention                                                                            |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| routes/          | One `defineHandler` per file: `greeting.get.ts` answers `GET /api/v1/greeting`.       |
| mcp/tools/       | `defineTool` modules only MCP serves, named by their file.                            |
| pages/           | Fixed-path public response handlers; index.ts serves `/`.                             |
| middleware/      | Ordered HTTP wrappers or post-admission operation policy.                             |
| crons/           | A `cron` export and a default native scheduled handler.                               |
| queues/          | Default queue handlers named after the physical queue.                                |
| email/           | Default email handlers named after the full recipient; `_default.ts` is the fallback. |
| durable-objects/ | Default classes re-exported in PascalCase from kebab-case filenames.                  |
| db/              | Application-owned schemas and SQL migrations, applied explicitly.                     |
| src/             | Optional shared domain code; application configuration lives at the root.             |
| public/          | Optional static assets; configure the binding and admitted files before using it.     |
| .maximus/        | Generated imports; ignored and never edited by hand.                                  |

The Vite plugin reconciles modules on every build and source change.
Root maximus.config.ts owns application and transport policy; the Cloudflare config names the
generated .maximus/entry.ts entry. No src/ directory or manual route registration is required. `bun run prepare:project` generates the same imports for editors. Files starting
with `_` are ignored except `email/_default.ts`; `.dev.ts` and `.prod.ts` select their matching mode.
Platform bindings, cron triggers, queue subscriptions, email routing and Durable Object migrations
remain explicit Cloudflare configuration. Adding a handler never provisions infrastructure.

## Deployment

Before deploying, replace the origin and audience in maximus.config.ts with the deployed HTTPS URL.
The GitHub workflow checks pull requests and deploys pushes to `main`. Configure repository or
organization secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. The token needs permission to
deploy this Worker. `bun run deploy` performs the same non-test validation and deployment locally.

Vite+ owns the root toolchain: `vite.config.ts` configures lint/format, `vp check` checks them,
`vp build` bundles the Worker and `vp dev` runs it locally. TypeScript and Cloudflare type generation
remain part of `bun run verify`. Tests are never part of automatic deployment.
